    "updated_at": "2017-10-06T19:22:46Z",
    "body": "I guess the actual part of the spec you are asking about is https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/text-level-semantics.html#the-a-element:attr-img-ismap ?\r\n\r\nIs there a particular reason for special-casing javascript: URLs here? My thought is that we should just use the same code, no matter the URL scheme, and if that results in a nonsensical result, then oh well.\r\n\r\nOtherwise we have to start questioning things like, does it make sense to append to data: or blob: URLs? What about ftp:, where (from what I understand) there are no query strings involved? What about file:, where there is no server to interpret the query strings?\r\n\r\nIt seems better to just use uniform logic everywhere.",
